{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For yet seven days.</b> For on the seventh day I will cause it to rain until the end of forty days — now this was on the tenth of the second month, and at the end of the forty days from the beginning the middle one will return to straight, and it is a sod," "And the word היקום — we do not find it except in this pericope, and its root is among the verbs whose pe letter is not whole, on the pattern of כרוב. And some say it is among the verbs whose ayin is a weak letter [נחי העין], and it is the opposite of \"as YHWH pleads [יריב] against my adversaries [יריבי]\" (Psalms 35:1). And the word יקום is a general term for every living thing that is upon the earth."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "Resolved היקום/יקום as the forms Ibn Ezra discusses; left his grammatical terms (pe letter, weak letter [נחי העין]) technical per voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:38.245301520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}